N1  - <p>BOINC criterion evidence - Abstract, verbatim: "To avoid high workloads for the control computer of the CrystalMation system, the computing is distributed over several workstations, participating voluntarily, by the grid programming system from the Berkeley Open Infrastructure for Network Computing (BOINC)." Section 2.4, verbatim: "In order to ensure the unrestricted operation of a program on the computers of volunteers, executables for all used operating systems must be provided on the BOINC server." Section 2.4: "The BOINC server comes by default with the core components scheduler, feeder, transitioner, validator, assimilator and file deleter." Section 3.2: "To reach this grade of image processing rate BOINC was employed to guarantee a real-time processing of the images." | Full text: Acta Cryst. A79(Part 4):331-338 (2023), Open Access CC BY 4.0 | Link: Crystal Search / BOINC | Source: IUCr (2023)ER&nbsp;&nbsp;-</p>
